 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTeradata property parsing returns None instead of parsing properties\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing Teradata SQL with properties, the parser incorrectly returns `None` for all properties instead of properly parsing them. This affects CREATE TABLE statements and other DDL that include Teradata-specific properties.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import parse_one\n\n# This should parse Teradata properties but returns None\nsql = \"\"\"\nCREATE SET TABLE test, NO FALLBACK, NO BEFORE JOURNAL, NO AFTER JOURNAL,\nCHECKSUM = DEFAULT (x INT, y INT, z CHAR(30), a INT, b DATE, e INT)\nPRIMARY INDEX (a),\nINDEX(x, y)\n\"\"\"\n\nparsed = parse_one(sql, dialect='teradata')\nprint(\"Parsed successfully:\", parsed is not None)\n\n# Properties should be parsed but are missing\nproperties = parsed.find_all(sqlglot.expressions.Property)\nprint(\"Found properties:\", len(list(properties)))\n```\n\nExpected: Properties like `NO FALLBACK`, `NO BEFORE JOURNAL`, etc. should be parsed and available in the AST.\nActual: Properties are not parsed correctly, resulting in incomplete parsing of Teradata DDL statements.\n</issue>\n",
